      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T08:46:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Have looked into it and discussed with remi.\nThe issue here is shellCommand() requires the caller to have UID root or UID shell. https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/Binder.java;l\u003d1251;drc\u003d06bd5d4af5ec3ac61904303953b6f96bdf6eae4c;bpv\u003d0;bpt\u003d1\n\nIf we want to do it in CTS, we need to spawn a shell.\n\nAlso, the benefit for using binder.shellCommand() is we don\u0027t need to hardcoded string \"network_stack\". The \"apf $wifiIfaceName capabilities\" string is still needed to be hardcoded.\n\nIt seems the benefit is very minimal?",
